{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-23638" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039367/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a0251ede3323a692c69fc666221a7a4706396575650c6f4421a0566dc7c57bd"} {"question" "q-23638" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nWe now simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following identities:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta },\\,\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the above identities, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039367/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a0251ede3323a692c69fc666221a7a4706396575650c6f4421a0566dc7c57bd"} {"question" "q-23638" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039367/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0798ece5d0a2d260a2cf373eb2ea5bd6dc4b3fe91cf175ef36215808cc370b63"} {"question" "q-23638" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039367/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a0251ede3323a692c69fc666221a7a4706396575650c6f4421a0566dc7c57bd"} {"question" "q-23638" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039367/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a0251ede3323a692c69fc666221a7a4706396575650c6f4421a0566dc7c57bd"} {"question" "q-23638" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039367/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a02